 * Occurrence days are `YYYY-MM-DD` strings and are only ever compared as
 * calendar days, never as instants: "day D has started" means the wall clock
 * in the rule's own time zone has reached 00:00 on D. Because a wall clock
 * only shows date D once it has reached D 00:00 (a spring-forward gap that
 * swallows midnight jumps straight past it), that is the same as "the local
 * date is at least D" — which keeps daylight-saving shifts out of the maths.
 */

